-	// against the live queue is what made capturing three REQs fail this test;
-	// the fixed payload above (timelineFixedFixturePayloadScript) now pins the
-	// refusal regime, so the enabled branch below is not reachable on this board.
-	// It stays because the contract is the same in both regimes and is stated
-	// here as one: the arrow's own verdict is READ and the press is checked
-	// against it — it never lands the reader on an empty chart, and whatever it
-	// is about to do it says first. The refusal is exercised a second time under
